From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0814: resolve_reinterpret_reload: scaled textures outdated only by another surface's resolves keep their data; resolve_elide's keep rules match depth resolves; reinterpreting reads keep nothing (Direct3D 12; native stream, zero-copy session 2 B)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (native stream; scratch/zerocopy2/DESIGN2.md section B, TESTPLAN2.md). Written without a build or
  a run: checked with clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only (the SDK's Release flags) of d3d12/resolve_elide.cpp, d3d12/texture_cache.cpp,
  d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp, command_processor.cpp, pipeline/texture/cache.cpp and the units that include the changed headers;
  0 errors, no warning on an added line. Needs 0813 (applies after it) and 0810.
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: Session 1's 0810 learn and elide runs.
  1. A MISS on a destination its keep rule names (0x06CEE000 fmt 23 src 4): for a depth resolve draw_util::GetResolveInfo replaces
     the destination format with the depth target's texture format (draw.cpp: k_24_8 / k_24_8_FLOAT, 22 / 23), which resolve_elide's
     key and printed rules carry, while CommandProcessor::MatchResolveScaledBytesReader read the RB_COPY_DEST_INFO register (left at
     anything by the title for a depth copy): no depth rule ever matched. The keep rules now match the key's format (the
     unscaled-copy and readback rules stay on the registers, as IssueCopy matches them).
  2. The reloads every frame: the 24 MB depth-as-8888 texture at 0x06CEE000 is outdated after its whole dual write by the 256x256,
     224x220 and 64x32 resolves (pitch 256 / 224 / 64) into the same 6.5 MB; the 640x640 shadow atlas at 0x0732E000 by the 800x500
     16F resolve at its base, after which its partial dual write cannot make it up to date. New cvar resolve_reinterpret_reload (int,
     default 0 = as before, hot reload): every scaled resolve is logged (a ring of 1024: extent, pitch, bytes a texel, the texture it
     dual-wrote) and every scaled texture remembers the resolve count as of which it is up to date; a texture whose resolves since
     are all of another pitch or texel size (reinterpretations) or dual writes into itself is, with 1, not loaded (it keeps its data);
     with 2 it is loaded with those resolves' bytes poisoned. Loaded as before: no known state, a CPU write since (a new flag of the
     base Texture, from its watch), history out of the ring, a resolve of its own layout, no resolve at all.
  3. A load by a texture of another pitch or texel size than a store's is no reader of that store for resolve_elide (no keep, no
     miss: on the console it reads another surface's bytes); a partial dual write into an outdated texture is elided when the reload
     decision says that texture will not be loaded. resolve_elide_after and resolve_elide_min_kb default to 0 (all sizes, no
     warm-up). `[resolve-reload] ...` every 10 s while resolve_reinterpret_reload is on.
Bucket: REDO

0814-resolve-reinterpret-reload.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, zero-copy session 2).

